56,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Minato,,The Woodland Walk seems peaceful. But will the trees be okay in the clay soil?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, look at the costs! Woodland means high upkeep per hectare. The Market Plaza is mostly paving. That's the only one that won't bleed us dry.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I fear the Woodland Walk will suffer the same fate as the eastern avenue. So many trees, but who will water them?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The Market Plaza requires the least daily gardening, but the Sports Terraces would put more pressure on the already thin staff for cleaning and management.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the Market Plaza is just a giant heat-sink. We already have heat readings that are too high. Paving the park is a disaster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, you're right. Paving sounds hot. What about the Wetland Restoration? It sounds like it helps with the drainage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, wetlands are a nightmare to maintain. Specialized care, bought-in services... it's a financial black hole. I'm sticking with the Plaza.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,The Wetland Restoration is very thoughtful. It works with the water rather than fighting it. It feels more honest to the land.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"The Wetland plan is complex. It requires specific knowledge. If our staff is gone, we'd be entirely dependent on expensive contractors.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the Wetland plan is the only one that doesn't ignore the drainage callouts. Plus, it doesn't block the tram-commuter paths like the Woodland Walk would.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I like the idea of the water. It sounds soothing. And if it helps the drainage, maybe the firms won't be as worried?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,You're all so romantic. I'm the only one thinking about the budget. The Plaza is the only one that doesn't require a gardening army.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, dear, a park that is just a plaza is not a park. I would rather have a wetland that we learn to care for than a concrete square.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I am torn. The Plaza is easy on the staff, but the Wetland is better for the city. However, the staff rota is already too short.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, a wetland is a self-regulating system if done right. It's far more rational than a ""Woodland"" that dies or a ""Plaza"" that cooks the pedestrians.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I think I'll go with the Wetland. It seems the most helpful for the ground.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I'm staying with the Plaza. I won't vote for a plan that costs a fortune to keep.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Minato and Shunichi. Let us choose the Wetland. It is a gentle way to fix the drainage.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I cannot support the Woodland or Sports plans. Between the Plaza and the Wetland, the Plaza is safer for the staff, but the Wetland is the only one that makes sense for the land. I'll choose the Wetland.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Finally, some logic. The Wetland is the only choice that doesn't fight the reality of the site.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
